  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: We have only one completed experiment (config_001, rna_only/singleprofile/pca_n2000) with a low baseline accuracy of 0.485 and F1 of 0.464, leaving substantial uncertainty about which modality and design choices drive performance. Question: Does the image modality alone carry meaningful predictive signal for cellular profiling? config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is structurally parallel to config_001 (singleprofile, no aggregation, no fusion), making it a clean single-variable comparison that isolates the modality effect. Why best next step: Before committing budget to multimodal fusion or more complex encoders, establishing the image-only ceiling is the highest-information experiment. If image_only substantially outperforms or underperforms RNA-only, it immediately informs whether multimodal fusion is worthwhile, which image encoder to prioritize, and whether the RNA or image branch needs more attention. This reduces the most fundamental uncertainty with a single experiment, making every subsequent multimodal result interpretable."
}

